# i18n rules

v1 ships English only, but every user-visible string goes through `t()` so we can drop in French and Arabic later without a refactor.

## Hard rules

- **No string literals in JSX or alerts.** Use `t('namespace.key')`.
- **All keys live in `apps/mobile/src/i18n/locales/<lang>.json`.** Currently only `en.json`.
- **New strings: add the key to every locale file** (English now, but the structure is in place).
- **Keep keys hierarchical**: `lobby.create.title`, `game.action.callPablo`, `error.network.offline`.
- **No string concatenation** for translated content. Use ICU MessageFormat / interpolation: `t('game.scoreLine', { name, score })`.

## When RTL eventually matters

When we add Arabic, layouts must respect RTL. Use logical properties already (`paddingStart`, `marginEnd`) instead of `paddingLeft`/`marginRight`. Cheap to do now, expensive to retrofit.

## Example

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Button title="Call Pablo" />
<Text>{`Score: ${score}`}</Text>

// ✅ GOOD
<Button title={t('game.action.callPablo')} />
<Text>{t('game.scoreLine', { score })}</Text>
```
